---
title: German Apple Cake
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: German
---

= Cake Mixture =

Combine @sugar{110%g}, @self-raising flour{140%g}, @salt{pinch}, @butter{110%g}(melted), @egg{1}(beaten) for the cake mixture.

= Filling =

Mix @apples{450%g}(approx. 3 bramleys, peeled and chopped), @sultanas{55%g}, @walnuts{28%g}, @cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, and @demerara sugar{55%g} for the filling.

= Assemble and Bake =

Place two-thirds of the cake mixture in the bottom of a cake tin. Cover with the filling. Put the rest of the cake mixture on top in spoonfuls.

Preheat the oven to 180°C (160°C fan). Bake for ~{1%hour} in the centre of the oven.

Leave in the tin until cold.